{"type":"message","id":"3bc6ef50","parentId":"fc98fd15","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:03:25.894Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API seems to return the same \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" for any request. The 1101 error on POST might be because the server doesn't accept POST on /send. \n\nLet me check if maybe the history endpoint can give me more information about the API structure, and maybe there's a different endpoint for posting.\n\nWait - the root endpoint returns \"Unauthorized\" but /send?threadId=... returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" regardless of method. And POST returns 1101. The 1101 error from Cloudflare Workers could be because the worker is rejecting the request due to validation.\n\nActually wait - the GET to /history?threadId=...&limit=5 works fine and returns real data. \n\nSo /send might have specific validation requirements. The 1101 error is a Cloudflare Workers error indicating request validation failure - maybe the Content-Type or API key format is wrong, or the body is too large. Let me check if there's a size limit by testing with a minimal payload first.","thinkingSignature":"b65ea3f09a98d44153e4fb76e3540e1794c4e1f949aced1c8424affe192e4a7c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_jousp274yivh_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if maybe content type is the issue\ncurl -v -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":9814,"output":329,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23825,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780311799270,"responseId":"066c99f7c3b20fb16aadec15f9859088"}}
