{"type":"message","id":"b418b26c","parentId":"9e113eb7","timestamp":"2026-06-01T11:03:37.000Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'm getting \"Unauthorized\" instead of 1101. So the API key format matters. The original X-API-KEY header worked for GET endpoints. Let me try with the original header format but different content. \n\nActually, looking at the pattern:\n- GET with X-API-KEY: *** (returns data)\n- POST with X-API-KEY + JSON: returns 1101 (500 error)\n- POST with apiKey query param: returns \"Unauthorized\"\n- POST with Authorization header: returns \"Unauthorized\"\n\nSo the X-API-KEY header is correct, but POST fails with 1101. This could be:\n1. The POST endpoint is broken","thinkingSignature":"9db02ce958da5d4df01579f98a318805d1ba874345fe3a15f6f970f132badb3a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cpfyzpu6q31f_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with very short content\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"ping\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":10788,"output":233,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24703,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780311812686,"responseId":"066c9a056733930f7e07aede43da0e1f"}}
